
        BLACKJACK (PYTHON)
================================================================================

A simple command-line Blackjack game written in Python. Play against the computer,
try to get as close to 21 as possible without going over,
and see who wins each round.


================================================================================
FEATURES
================================================================================
- Classic Blackjack gameplay against a computer dealer
- Optional rules screen before starting a game
- Automatic Ace handling (11 -> 1) to avoid busting
- Natural Blackjack detection (Ace + 10-value card in two cards)
- Dealer follows the standard "hit until 17" rule
- Replayable rounds - keep playing as long as you like
- Emoji-based result messages for a bit of fun


================================================================================
REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================
- Python 3.6+
- No third-party packages required.
  Only the standard library (random) is used.


================================================================================
PROJECT STRUCTURE
================================================================================
.
|-- main.py          Main game file (the code you provided)
|-- art.py           Contains the `logo` ASCII art variable
|-- rules.py         Contains the `rulebook` string with rules text
|-- README.txt       This file

NOTE: art.py and rules.py are imported at the top of main.py.
You must create these files (or remove the imports and their
usages) for the game to run.


================================================================================
HOW TO RUN
================================================================================
1. Make sure main.py, art.py, and rules.py are all in
   the same directory.
2. Open a terminal in that directory.
3. Run:

       python main.py


================================================================================
HOW TO PLAY
================================================================================
When the game starts, you'll be prompted:

    Do you want to play a game of Blackjack? Type 'yes' or 'no':

- Type 'yes' to start.
- You'll then be asked whether you want to read the rules first.
- During the round, type 'yes' to draw another card ("hit")
  or 'no' to keep your hand ("stand").

SPECIAL SCORE VALUES
--------------------
  Score    Meaning
  -------  --------------------------------------------
  0        Natural Blackjack (Ace + 10-value in 2 cards)
  < 21     Under - still in the game
  21       Perfect score (via more than two cards)
  > 21     Bust - you lose immediately


================================================================================
GAME RULES
================================================================================
1. Both the player and the computer are dealt two cards
   at the start.
2. Number cards are worth their face value; face cards
   are worth 10; an Ace is worth 11 (or 1 if it would
   cause a bust).
3. A two-card hand totaling 21 is a "Blackjack".
4. The player may draw additional cards or stand at
   any point.
5. The computer (dealer) keeps drawing cards until its
   score is 17 or higher.
6. The winner is decided by compare():
   - Equal scores        -> Draw
   - Player busts        -> Player loses
   - Player has Blackjack-> Player wins
   - Dealer busts        -> Player wins
   - Dealer has Blackjack-> Player loses
   - Player's score higher -> Player wins
   - Otherwise           -> Player loses


================================================================================
CODE OVERVIEW
================================================================================
  Function                     Purpose
  ---------------------------  --------------------------------
  deal_card()                  Returns a random card from the deck.
  calculate_score(cards)       Computes the hand's total score,
                               handling Aces and Blackjack detection.
  compare(u_score, c_score)    Compares player and dealer scores,
                               returns the result message.
  game_on()                    Runs one full round: dealing, player
                               turn, dealer turn, and result.

The main loop at the bottom of the file keeps the game running
until the user answers 'no'.


================================================================================
EXAMPLE GAMEPLAY
================================================================================
    Do you want to play a game of Blackjack? Type 'yes' or 'no': yes
    Do you want to read the rules first? Type 'yes' or 'no': no

    Your cards: [10, 7], current score: 17
    Computer's first card: 9
    Type 'yes' to get another card, type 'no' to pass: no
    Your final hand: [10, 7], final score: 17
    Computer's final hand: [9, 8], final score: 17
    Draw.


